    "result_text": "The quick-add bar is in, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests: the new quick-add test and the three existing scenarios.\n\n**What it does:** the bar sits on the people list. It has a name field, an amount field and an \"Add claim\" button. It adds a DRAFT claim for that amount, dated the sheet's today, with an empty note.\n- The name is trimmed and matched without regard to case, so \" dot \" finds Dot.\n- If no one on the sheet has that name, the person is added first with grade A. The audit file then gets `PERSON_ADDED`, that person's `ROLLUP` line, and then `CLAIM_ADDED`, in that order, which is what the test expects.\n\n**Refusals:** a blank name, a bad amount (missing, negative or more than two decimals), or a today that falls in a closed period all show the bar's error. All of these checks run before anything is written, so a refused quick-add adds no person, stores no claim and writes no audit line. The error clears when you edit either field or submit again.\n\n**Changes:**\n- New endpoint `POST /api/sheets/{sheetId}/quick-add` (`quick-add.POST.yml`), with new step classes in the `claim` package: `ValidateQuickAdd`, `CheckQuickAddOpen` and `ResolveQuickPerson`. After those it reuses the existing claim-creation, audit and rollup steps.\n- `ValidateClaim`: I moved its rules into a shared helper so the bar applies exactly the same amount rules as the claim form. The claim form behaves as before.\n- `PersonRepository`: added `findByName`, which matches names without regard to case.\n- `People.tsx`: added the `QuickAdd` component.\n\nOne edge case is untested: if two users quick-add the same new name at the same moment, the database's unique-name rule rejects the second one. That shows the bar's generic error rather than a specific message, and nothing is written. The existing add-person form already behaves the same way in that case.",
